invariant: INV-48
file: mldsa_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mldsa-avx2
reason: the four-way sampler hands each state rho || i || j, where FIPS
  204 Algorithm 32 gives rho || j || i, so a session with CH_CPU_AVX2
  samples another matrix and no honest signature verifies. Only an x86-64
  compiler reads the line, so the script builds bin/mldsa_avx2_equiv_test
  for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without
  docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
        x1[k] = (uint8_t)i;
--- new
        x1[k] = x0[k];
        x0[k] = (uint8_t)i;
